  "description": "Buildings the player places (city building P0-A, ARCHITECTURE decision 92) in a world 20480 x 20480 units (320 m). A building is a square, its sides north-south and east-west, of its kind's side: a house 1024 (16 m), a shop 1536, an office block 2048; it covers centre - side / 2 up to (not including) centre + side / 2 each way, at any point of the world (the 64 m cells do not bind it). It is placed free of charge and houses no one yet. A house at (5000, 5000) covers 4488 to 5512 each way and is building 1. A shop at (6280, 5000) covers 5512 to 7048 east-west: it touches the house and shares no ground, so it is building 2. An office block at (6000, 5000) would cover 4976 to 7024 and share ground with both: buildingOverlaps names the lower, 1. A house at (511, 5000) would reach x = -1: outOfBounds names its centre. A straight edge from (2000, 10000) to (18000, 10000) (16000 units, 16 pricing lengths of 1024 rounded up, 1600) is edge 1. A building keeps 128 (2 m) from a track's centre line: a house at (6000, 9361) reaches 9873, 127 from the line, buildingOnTrack names edge 1; at (6000, 9360) it reaches 9872, exactly 128 away, and is building 3. Market (1000) stands at (12000, 6000). An office block at (12000, 7151) would start at y = 6127, 127 from the station's point: buildingOnStation names station 1; at (12000, 7152) it starts at 6128, 128 away, and is building 4. Building 5 does not exist. The balance: 10000 - 1600 - 1000 = 7400. Every value worked out by hand.",
